1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,148
Faultline: an on-call agent whose brain is a FalkorDB graph. The model suggests; a read-only query decides.

2
00:00:06,148 --> 00:00:11,003
Re-arm: restore the tenant graph from its golden copy and reset the simulated GitHub world.

3
00:00:11,003 --> 00:00:20,006
Run S1, “Checkout errors are spiking”, with the keyless baseline investigator: the stage rail moves INTAKE → RECALL → …

4
00:00:20,006 --> 00:00:28,002
First it remembers: past payment incidents found in FalkorDB's vector index and confirmed through a shared symptom node, never similarity alone.

5
00:00:28,002 --> 00:00:36,001
algo.BFS shows what breaks: payment red, the blast radius yellow, hop by hop.

6
00:00:36,001 --> 00:00:48,412
Three changes in the window. The recommendation deploy has no causal path to checkout: Q-GATE-1 returns 0 rows. No path, no claim.

7
00:00:48,412 --> 00:00:58,000
The email deploy shipped in the same minute and has a path. But algo.maxFlow says it carries at most 0.0200; 0.2433 is needed. Rejected, with proof.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:11,305
algo.SPpaths: D-pay-417 → payment → checkout, lit edge by edge. Every claim carries its Cypher, with PROFILE engine time.

9
00:01:11,305 --> 00:01:16,819
Same graph, data incident (recorded replay): a payment provider cutover, traced into the revenue lineage.

10
00:01:16,819 --> 00:01:22,048
Same graph, data incident (recorded replay): the path crosses into the revenue lineage; the stale FX feed is ruled out by flow (0.0692 < 0.8000).

11
00:01:22,048 --> 00:01:26,530
Better still: the same graph scores the risky pull request before it ships: verdict, the ADRs it contradicts, the path to checkout, reviewers.

12
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:36,057
Preflight verdict: block. The same graph that explained the outage gates the next change before it merges.

13
00:01:36,057 --> 00:01:45,000
Back to the incident. algo.maxFlow finds the smallest cut; a what-if on a GRAPH.COPY branch checks that it contains the failure first.

14
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:53,001
Who fixes it: the people who wrote this code and fixed the last outages here, ranked by harmonic centrality; bus factor and escalation tree.

15
00:01:53,001 --> 00:02:03,000
Choosing isn't approving: the server renders the exact diff, the PR body with reviewers, and the plan hash first.

16
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,058
Approve this exact change: one PR (simulated GitHub, labelled), verified through a second channel, then written back.

17
00:02:07,058 --> 00:02:17,799
APPLIED: GitHub main re-read and telemetry back in band, no collateral. Write-back verified 7/7; the incident becomes memory.

18
00:02:17,799 --> 00:02:27,051
And when verification can't confirm the change (S9, an eval run): verdict UNKNOWN, success written = False. Never a silent success: a later reconciler pass → at_main, APPLIED 7/7. (evals/RESULTS.md)

19
00:02:27,051 --> 00:02:38,816
And it's the team's memory: every node an answer cites was read by that question's own queries, or the answer is withheld.

20
00:02:38,816 --> 00:02:47,049
FalkorDB off (A4): 0 confirmed causes. Max-flow check off (A3-noG5): top-1 0.8. S2 can no longer be decided (0.0); S1 still is (1.0): the sweep's origin test rejects the healthy email service.

21
00:02:47,049 --> 00:02:55,032
Vector similarity only (V): top-1 0.4; it picks the wrong change on S2, S3 and S3b. Naive recency: 0.1. The graph (A3): 1.0. (evals/RESULTS.md)

22
00:02:55,032 --> 00:02:59,001
Faultline: no path, no claim. Verify it yourself: make judge-check.

